<title>USA: U.S. JOBLESS CLAIMS ROSE IN LATEST WEEK.</title>
<headline>U.S. JOBLESS CLAIMS ROSE IN LATEST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Labor Department report of initial state jobless benefit claims, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>Week Ended Initial Claims  4-Week Avg.  Continued Claims   - 08/02/97     300,000	303,750	Unavailable</p>
<p>  - 07/26/97     275,000-R    325,250-R    2,352,000</p>
<p>  - 07/19/97     299,000	340,750	2,320,000-R</p>
<p>  - 07/12/97     341,000	349,000	2,330,000-R</p>
<p>R-Revised, July 26 Initial Claims from 277,000; July 26 Four-Week Average from 325,750; July 19 Continued Claims from 2,335,000 and July 12 from 2,333,000.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast initial jobless claims</p>
</text>
